# Copy to .dev.vars for `npm run dev`. These are Cloudflare's published test
# values, not secrets — the real key is set with `wrangler secret put`.
#
# Turnstile test keys (https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/):
#   1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA  always passes
#   2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA  always fails
# Pair them with the matching test site key in apps/scheduler/index.html:
#   1x00000000000000000000AA  always passes
#   2x00000000000000000000AB  always fails
# The production site key only renders on nuclearcyborg.com — on 127.0.0.1 it
# fails with Turnstile error 110200 ("domain not authorized"), which is the
# widget working as configured, not a bug. Swap both halves for the test pair
# above to work locally. Do NOT add 127.0.0.1 to the production widget's
# hostname list: the site key is public, so allowing loopback would let anyone
# mint valid tokens for it from their own machine.
TURNSTILE_SECRET="1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA"

# Tokens from the test keys report hostname "example.com"; production expects
# nuclearcyborg.com (set in wrangler.jsonc). Override it here for local runs.
TURNSTILE_HOSTNAME="example.com"
